From u574beeebc8eda76a at groups.google.com  Tue May 30 14:25:49 2023
From: u574beeebc8eda76a at groups.google.com (Philemon Cyclone)
Date: Tue, 30 May 2023 14:25:49 +0000
Subject: Clarification on 'first-available' resource selection
Message-ID: <EKxA4sP_-Fs.bgKJm_APCQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/EKxA4sP_-Fs/m/bgKJm_APCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I was wondering if you could please clarify how the 'first-available' selection policy works, specifically in terms of what conditions are checked to determine "first-available".

Does this look only at the resource capacity schedule (i.e., the first resource to have capacity >0) or does it also look at which resource will first have queue count = 0? How does the selection work if multiple resources are provided that are tied for capacity, server, and queue counts?

Thank you.

From u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com  Tue May 30 19:44:54 2023
From: u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?q?I=C3=B1aki_Ucar?=)
Date: Tue, 30 May 2023 19:44:54 +0000
Subject: Re: [simmer-devel] Clarification on 'first-available' resource selection
Message-ID: <EKxA4sP_-Fs.bFh9QlohCQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <EKxA4sP_-Fs.bgKJm_APCQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
References: <EKxA4sP_-Fs.bgKJm_APCQAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/EKxA4sP_-Fs/m/bFh9QlohCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first-available policy checks the resources in the order given, and selects the first one with a server count that is less than the capacity. If all resources are busy, then it selects the first one with space in the queue. You can check the logic here <https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/blob/cb9b0651d1c7b6fa364fee708407ec6b4619a2d3/inst/include/simmer/activity/resource_internal.h#L132>.

Iñaki

